      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sync): add quiet presence mode",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add `wacli sync --presence-mode normal|quiet`, defaulting to `normal`.\n- Preserve current sync presence behaviour by default.\n- In `quiet` mode, suppress available presence on authenticated connect, connect events, and push-name updates while still sending unavailable presence on cleanup.\n- Document the personal mirror use case and add presence-mode tests.\n\n## Why\n\nLong-running `sync --follow` sessions can keep the linked device globally available. For personal-number mirror deployments, that can interfere with primary phone notification behaviour. Quiet mode gives operators an explicit opt-in that avoids available-presence updates without weakening the existing cleanup safety.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `CGO_ENABLED=1 CGO_CFLAGS=\"-Wno-error=missing-braces\" go test -tags sqlite_fts5 ./internal/app ./internal/wa ./cmd/wacli`\n- `pnpm format:check && pnpm lint && pnpm test && pnpm build` in an unprivileged copy at `/tmp/wacli-gate`\n- Built `./dist/wacli` and ran a redacted live one-shot sync against an authenticated personal mirror store with quiet mode:\n\n```text\n$ ./dist/wacli --store REDACTED --events sync --once --idle-exit 5s --max-reconnect 30s --presence-mode quiet --max-messages 50000 --max-db-size 1GB\nMessages stored: 0\n{\"event\":\"connected\",\"ts\":1783595268235}\n{\"event\":\"idle_exit\",\"data\":{\"idle_duration\":\"5s\",\"messages_synced\":0},\"ts\":1783595273510}\n\n$ ./dist/wacli --json --store REDACTED doctor\n{\"lock_held\":false,\"authenticated\":true,\"connected\":false,\"connection_state\":\"disconnected\"}\n```\n\nNote: the same full gate fails when run as root in `/root/clawd/repos/wacli` because `internal/fsutil` correctly expects chmod `0500` to be non-writable, but root can still write. The unprivileged run passes.\n\nCloses #297\n",
        "branch": "feat/sync-presence-mode",
